{
  "requirement": "Source providers can override parsing, text search, and structural search.\nThe SDK supplies defaults for all three, so listing, reading, and a supplied\nlanguage registry suffice to support them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations from the text**\n1. Providers can override parsing, text search, and structural search.\n2. The SDK supplies defaults for all three.\n3. A provider that implements only listing and reading, plus a supplied language registry, is enough to support all three.\n\n**Default text search.** `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` uses `Memory`, which implements only `list` and `read`. It calls the default `search_text` and asserts:\n- the result is complete;\n- there are two matches;\n- the first match reports the expected line;\n- the excerpt includes context;\n- the sequence of `list` and `read` calls on the provider is as expected.\n\n**Default parse.** The same test calls the default `parse` through `Memory` and asserts the parse snapshot's text and outline. It also checks that the parse reads the source once.\n\n**Default structural search from list and read only.** `list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search` uses `Primitives`, which supplies only listing and reading. It asserts:\n- `parse` works with the registry's language;\n- `search_structure` returns the expected selector, excerpt and resource;\n- a non-matching language gives an empty, complete result;\n- an unknown language and a malformed rule give errors;\n- an explicit language wins over the location's extension, and the extension is used when no language is given.\n\n**Overrides.** `structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope` uses `CachedParse`, which overrides `parse`. The default `search_structure` runs through that override, and the test asserts the override's parse count and the results under three limits. The `SourceProvider` trait declares `search_text` and `search_structure` as default methods that delegate to the `defaults` module. Overriding them is ordinary Rust trait-method overriding, with no conditional or transformation. `SourceAnalysis::search_structure` calls `self.provider.search_structure`, so an override takes effect. No test overrides `search_text` or `search_structure` directly. I treat this as exempt: the code is pass-through delegation, and the parse override is exercised.\n\n**Other coverage.** The agent test `source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads` runs the default text search through `SourceTools` and `LocalSources`. It also checks the separation between discovery and delivered reads, which `provider_observations` covers.\n\nThe assertions enforce the outcomes, and I found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept. Delegated sub-requirements (`provider_defaults.composition` and `provider_results`) are also marked on these tests and are not reassessed here.",
